Test files in this folder
=========================

Every .xls file in this folder and in fuzz/ (calamine/ is described below)
comes unchanged from the test data of Apache POI (test-data/spreadsheet in
https://github.com/apache/poi), which is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0:
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The function table in src/formula/functions.rs comes from Apache POI too;
see the crate's NOTICE.

Apache POI's NOTICE file says:

    Apache POI
    Copyright 2003-2026 The Apache Software Foundation

    This product includes software developed at
    The Apache Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/).

The files in fuzz/ are inputs that broke Apache POI's own reader (minimized
by OSS-Fuzz); here they check that damaged files fail cleanly.

Files by BIFF version
---------------------

BIFF3 (Excel 3.0, raw stream): testEXCEL_3.xls
BIFF4 (Excel 4.0, raw stream): testEXCEL_4.xls
BIFF5 (Excel 5.0/95, "Book" stream): testEXCEL_5.xls, testEXCEL_95.xls,
  59074.xls, 64130.xls (Excel for the Mac, Mac Roman, chart only)
BIFF8 (Excel 97-2003): everything else. Notable ones:
  1904DateWindowing.xls       1904 date system
  chinese-provinces.xls       Chinese text in the SST
  61287.xls                   Chinese sheet name, merged cells
  DBCSSheetName.xls           Hindi sheet names
  unicodeNameRecord.xls       Japanese defined name
  shared_formulas.xls, SharedFormulaTest.xls, overlapSharedFormula.xls,
  AbnormalSharedFormulaFlag.xls  shared formulas, including odd anchors
  testArraysAndTables.xls     array formulas and what-if data tables
  3dFormulas.xls, 55906-MultiSheetRefs.xls  3D references
  externalFunctionExample.xls, XRefCalc.xls, 49612.xls  external names
  61045_govdocs1_626534.xls   FORMAT records cut short by their writer; POI
                              took it from the Govdocs1 corpus (Digital
                              Corpora: documents from US government web
                              sites)
  BOOK_in_capitals.xls        stream named "BOOK"
  WithChart.xls               embedded chart substream
  password.xls, xor-encryption-abc.xls  encrypted (FILEPASS)

BIFF2 (Excel 2.x) files are not in POI's test data. The tests build BIFF2
streams (and BIFF5 streams with East Asian code pages) in code instead; see
tests/synthetic.rs.

Files from calamine
-------------------

The .xls files in calamine/ come unchanged from the test data of calamine
0.37.0 (tests/ in https://github.com/tafia/calamine), which is licensed under
the MIT License: Copyright (c) 2016 Johann Tuffe. The full license text is in
calamine/LICENSE-MIT.

Most are bug reports against calamine's .xls reader:
  biff5_write.xls, misc_biff5_parsing.xls, issue_643_biff5_formula.xls
                              BIFF5 cells, names and formulas
  biff5-rich-text-string.xls  rich text in the SST (UTF-16 with symbols)
  sheet_name_parsing.xls      UTF-16 strings with CODEPAGE 1252
  date_east_asian.xls         East Asian date formats
  sst_continue.xls            SST split over CONTINUE records
  formula-utf16-string.xls    STRING record holding UTF-16 text
  empty-string.xls, malformed_format.xls, issue_577_dimensions_16_bytes.xls,
  ptgexp-truncated-operand.xls, xls_formula.xls  writer quirks
  OOM_alloc.xls, OOM_alloc2.xls, OOM_alloc3.xls, issue_714.xls, too_small.xls
                              damaged files that must fail cleanly or read
                              without huge allocations
